  "body": "Locates the part in an imported fixture, or the fixture on the part, by face and point mates (#561, part of #339). Branched from the fork's main (synced at v0.15.0) with upstream/main merged.\n\n## What changed\n**Solver:** `fixture_locate.rs`, with the pure solve in `fixture_locate_solve.rs`. It takes one to three mates in the fixture's setup frame: face–face, point–point, point-on-face and face-on-point. It returns one rigid transform and never touches the WCS.\n- **Order:** 3-2-1 fixturing. The first face mate opposes the normals by the shortest turn. The second turns the part about that normal. A third must already agree. Then each mate fixes the remaining free motion, in mate order.\n- **Nudge:** after the mates, a turn about the first fixture normal, then an X/Y/Z shift.\n- **Pick reader:** `pick/mate.rs` reuses `outward_normal` and `facets_centroid` (#187/#330).\n\n**Commands** (`commands/locate.rs`):\n- `LocatePart` moves the part through `MoveModel`, so the stock follows. In a turned setup (#326) it composes into `AlignPartToSetup` instead.\n- `LocateFixture` moves the fixture by the inverse, through `MoveFixture`.\n- `Locate` wraps both for the UI and MCP. Every locate is one undo step.\n\n**Refused by name at creation:**\n- **Bodies:** no fixture, the machine table, a model that isn't a fixture, no part, or a pick on the wrong body.\n- **Picks:** an edge or curved face, a zero-area face, or two mates on the same point or face.\n- **Solve:** faces that can't oppose, contradicting mates, zero mates or more than three, a non-finite nudge, or \"nothing would move\".\n\n**Interpenetration warns rather than refuses.** A sampled inside test (the fixture mesh's ray law) names the part, the fixture and a point.\n\n**UI:**\n- **Fixtures page:** a **Locate part…** verb on each row.\n- **Model page:** a locate row.\n- **Form:** Move the part / Move the fixture, Offset X/Y/Z, Turn, **Apply locate** (greyed with the solve's reason) and Remove last.\n- **Picks:** part first, then fixture, routed through the existing face and vertex picking.\n\n**MCP:** a `locate_part` tool. `list_features` accepts a fixture.\n\n## Choices that differ from the issue (decision file: `docs/decisions/561-locate-part-fixture.md`)\n- **A moved fixture doesn't mark the setup's ops stale.** That keeps the existing rule that workholding never stales a toolpath. The collision check re-judges live instead, and a test pins it. Moving the part does mark them stale, and undo clears it.\n- **Maintainer's call: in an unaligned setup the part moves through `MoveModel`.** That changes its document placement, so in a multi-setup document it also moves the part in the other setups, and their ops go stale and need regenerating. A translation-only setup alignment was avoided, because it would make the setup count as aligned and refuse every non-2D op. An alternative is to refuse a locate in an unaligned multi-setup document and point to aligning the setup first.\n- **Deferred:** point-pair mates don't turn the part (only face mates orient it); there's no preview before Apply; per-setup part placement for unaligned multi-setup documents.\n\n## How tested\n- **App `fixture_locate` (11):**\n  - a face mate makes the faces coplanar with opposed normals;\n  - floor, jaw and stop give a full location;\n  - the offset and turn are exact;\n  - LocateFixture moves the fixture, not the part;\n  - undo and redo;\n  - point mates;\n  - degenerate and conflicting picks are refused by name;\n  - the interpenetration warning;\n  - ops go stale and undo clears it;\n  - a moved fixture is re-judged live while the path stays fresh;\n  - the turned-setup case.\n- **MCP:** `mcp_setup::locate_part_seats_the_part_on_the_fixture_by_feature_ids`.\n- **UI:**\n  - `locate_tests`: apply a locate from the Fixtures page, with undo and redo; the Model page moves the fixture to the part;\n  - `fixture_rows`: the locate tools fit inside the pane on both pages;\n  - `structural.rs`: no locate draft is armed by default.\n- **Regressions:** `fixtures`, `fixture_ux`, `fixture_mesh`, `fixture_mesh_posed`, `setup_align`, `plane_align`, `commands_undo`, `project_roundtrip`, `mcp`, `mcp_setup` and `mcp_pick` all pass. ui lib passes 379 of 380; the failure is the headless-GPU test, which needs a graphics adapter this machine doesn't have. Clippy (app and ui, `-D warnings`) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nA GUI hands-on check (the picks in the viewport). That will be driven headless next.\n\nChangelog: Locate the part in an imported fixture (or the fixture on the part) by face/point mates - floor, jaw, stop - with an offset and turn, from the Fixtures and Model pages and MCP locate_part (#561)\n\nFixes #561\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
